 "old_path": null, "path": "backend/testing/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/fixtures/AzuriteRunner.kt", "status": "A"}], "other": [], "tests": ["backend/app/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/component/fileStorage/FileStorageAzureTest.kt", "backend/app/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/component/fileStorage/FileStorageAzuriteTest.kt", "backend/app/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/unit/configuration/FileStorageConfigurationTest.kt", "backend/data/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/unit/component/fileStorage/AzureFileStorageFactoryTest.kt"]}}
{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1792931340, "commit": "3f361208b8aca11efefca0e19f105716dc433775", "id": "tolgee-3f361208b8ac", "issue": {"body": "The `/tolgee subscribe` command accepts only one option. When you use two, the first option takes the rest of the text as its value, and the command fails.\n\nExample:\n\n```\n/tolgee subscribe 1 fr --on translation_changed --global false\n```\n\nResult: `Invalid parameter translation_changed --global false. Please check the parameter and try again.`\n\nThe order does not matter. `--global false --on translation_changed` fails the same way.\n\n## Cause\n\n`SlackSlashCommandController.optionsRegex`:\n\n```\n(--[\\w-]+)\\s+([\\w-,\\s]+)\n```\n\nThe value part `[\\w-,\\s]+` allows spaces and `-`, so it also matches the next `--option` and its value. Tested on the JVM:\n\n| Input | Parsed |\n|---|---|\n| `--on translation_changed --global false` | `--on` = `translation_changed --global false` |\n| `--global false --on translation_changed` | `--global` = `false --on translation_changed` |\n| `--on translation_changed` | `--on` = `translation_changed` (OK) |\n\n## Workaround\n\nRun one command per option:\n\n```\n/tolgee subscribe 1 fr --on translation_changed\n/tolgee subscribe 1 --global false\n```\n\n## Possible fix\n\nStop the value before the next `--`, for example `(--[\\w-]+)\\s+((?:(?!\\s--)[\\w,\\s])+)`, and trim the value. The value still needs to allow spaces for lists like `--on new_key, base_changed`. A unit test for `parseOptions` with two options would cover it.\n", "number": 3947, "title": "Slack: /tolgee subscribe fails when more than one option is used"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "ce078f0fbb87a17a9d3e3f8970dff6c2134edddc", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "tolgee", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 3, "code_lines": 71, "test_files": 3}, "subject": "fix: parse multiple options and any language tag in Slack slash commands (#3950)", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[48, 0], [250, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/development/testDataBuilder/data/SlackTestData.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[79, 6], [94, 1], [322, 2], [325, 3], [330, 2], [333, 2], [336, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "ee/backend/app/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/api/v2/controllers/slack/SlackSlashCommandController.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[66, 4], [77, 3], [88, 0], [120, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "ee/backend/app/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/service/slackIntegration/SlackConfigManageService.kt", "status": "M"}], "other": [], "tests": ["ee/backend/tests/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/api/v2/controllers/slack/SlackSlashCommandControllerTest.kt", "ee/backend/tests/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/service/slack/SlackConfigServiceTest.kt", "ee/backend/tests/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/slack/SlackSlashCommandParsingTest.kt"]}}
{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1792931328, "commit": "ce078f0fbb87a17a9d3e3f8970dff6c2134edddc", "id": "tolgee-ce078f0fbb87", "issue": {"body": "When a key is created with several translations at once, the Slack \"new key\" message shows every translation many times. With N translations it shows N × N language blocks instead of N.\n\nExample: a key created with 9 translations (base + 8 languages) gives 81 language blocks, plus the \"Open in Tolgee\" button. That is 82 attachments in one message.\n\nIt happens when the key is created through the API, the CLI or an import. Keys created in the UI usually start with only the base translation (1 × 1 = 1), so it is rarely seen.\n\nSlack allows at most 100 attachments in one message. So I think with 10 or more translations the message is not posted at all. I did not test this.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Subscribe a Slack channel to a project with `/tolgee subscribe <projectId>` (all events).\n2. Create a key with translations in several languages in one request:\n   `POST /v2/projects/{projectId}/keys/create` with `{\"name\": \"some.key\", \"translations\": {\"en\": \"...\", \"de\": \"...\", \"fr\": \"...\", ...}}`\n3. The \"has created a new key\" message in the channel repeats each language N times.\n\n## Cause\n\n`SlackIntegrationDataProvider.getQuery()` joins the translations of a key with themselves:\n\n```\nFROM Translation t\n    join t.key k\n    join k.translations t2\nWHERE (t.key.id = :keyId or t.id = :translationId) ...\n```\n\nWhen searching by `translationId`, `t` is one row, so the result has N rows - correct. When searching by `keyId`, every translation of the key matches `t`, and each is joined with all N translations, so the result has N × N rows. `getKeyTranslations(keyId)` uses the `keyId` version, and `SlackOnKeyAddedMessageFactory` builds one attachment per row.\n\n## Possible fix\n\n- `SELECT DISTINCT new ...SlackTranslationInfoDto(...)`, or\n- a separate query for the `keyId` case: `FROM Translation t2 WHERE t2.key.id = :keyId`\n\nPlus a test that creates a key with several translations and checks the number of attachments.\n", "number": 3946, "title": "Slack: \"new key\" message repeats every translation when a key is created with many translations"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "dc09d9f1c9cce888a02193822f3a5f57a57903c4", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "tolgee", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 2, "code_lines": 19, "test_files": 1}, "subject": "fix: list each translation once in the Slack new key message (#3949)", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[34, 0], [138, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/development/testDataBuilder/data/SlackTestData.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[125, 6]], "old_path": null, "path": "ee/backend/app/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/component/slackIntegration/notification/SlackIntegrationDataProvider.kt", "status": "M"}], "other": [], "tests": ["ee/backend/tests/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/slack/SlackKeyAddedMessageTest.kt"]}}
{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1791214215, "commit": "ce04342dd2cfb6c969a8cb68c9828b20a98336f1", "id": "tolgee-ce04342dd2cf", "issue": {"body": "Currently, when a user exceeds their plan limits, only a small red circle appears in the dashboard header. This visual indicator is subtle and easy to miss\n\nDisplay a short, clear message next to the red circle (as shown in the screenshot below) \n\nSuggested Message: You've exceeded the limits of your plan\n\n<img width=\"566\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35e97659-b81d-4dc0-bf3f-1c9ee5ce5472\" />", "number": 3142, "title": "Improve visibility of plan limit on dashboard"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "0a5a8d878b65606102329b875b6a49162b803722", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "tolgee", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 7, "code_lines": 97, "test_files": 1}, "subject": "feat: show a top banner when the organization reaches its plan limit (#3898)", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[562, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "e2e/cypress/support/dataCyType.d.ts", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[16, 0], [29, 1], [68, 0], [74, 1], [86, 1], [88, 1], [96, 1], [109, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/component/layout/TopBanner/TopBanner.tsx", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[0, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/ee/billing/component/PlanLimitBanner.tsx", "status": "A"}, {"hunks": [[53, 0], [61, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/ee/billing/component/getProgressData.ts", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[81, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/ee/billing/limitPopover/generic/GenericPlanLimitPopover.tsx", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[102, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/eeSetup/eeModule.ee.tsx", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[86, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "webapp/src/eeSetup/eeModule.oss.tsx", "status": "M"}], "other": [], "tests": ["webapp/src/ee/billing/component/getProgressData.test.ts"]}}
{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1790585579, "commit": "8c6e11d68345b83d5a7d514ab1ed646f8002ce7e", "id": "tolgee-8c6e11d68345", "issue": {"body": "## Problem\n\nWhen auto-translate or \"pre-translate by TM\" finds several 100% matches for the same source text, the match that wins is arbitrary.\n\n`TmAutoTranslateProviderEeImpl.findExactMatch` runs a `union all` of stored entries and virtual rows and takes `limit 1`. The only ordering is `stored` before `virtual`. Between several virtual matches (same source text, different target text) there is no tiebreak, so Postgres returns whatever it scans first. Reviewed vs unreviewed, old vs new, all count the same.\n\nThe suggestion panel has the same gap. `AbstractTranslationMemoryService` orders by `similarity desc, assignmentPriority asc` and nothing else, so two 100% matches show up in random order.\n\n## Real case\n\nA project had two keys with the same source text. One had a correct target translation, the other had the source text copied into the target cell by a bad import. Auto-translate picked the wrong one for every new key with that source text. Preferring reviewed and then newest would have picked the correct one.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd a deterministic tiebreak to both queries, in this order:\n\n1. stored entries before virtual rows (as today)\n2. reviewed translations before unreviewed\n3. newest `updated_at` first\n\nSame order in the suggestion panel after `similarity desc, assignmentPriority asc`.\n\nThis will not fix data that is already wrong in every candidate, but it makes the choice predictable and picks the better value when one exists.\n", "number": 3913, "title": "Translation memory picks an arbitrary match when several 100% matches exist"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "3a42d977c564f4e1d7310c302ddbf7a13d2bcc61", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "tolgee", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 6, "code_lines": 99, "test_files": 1}, "subject": "fix: deterministic tiebreak for equal translation memory matches (#3920)", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[0, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/development/testDataBuilder/data/TranslationMemoryTiebreakTestData.kt", "status": "A"}, {"hunks": [[157, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/repository/TranslationRepository.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[45, 1], [47, 2], [50, 0], [96, 1], [108, 4], [148, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/service/translation/AbstractTranslationMemoryService.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[41, 1], [53, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "backend/data/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/service/translation/TranslationMemoryServiceOssImpl.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[101, 1], [115, 1], [143, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "ee/backend/app/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/service/translationMemory/TmAutoTranslateProviderEeImpl.kt", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[35, 1], [48, 1], [72, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "ee/backend/app/src/main/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/service/translationMemory/TranslationMemoryServiceEeImpl.kt", "status": "M"}], "other": [], "tests": ["ee/backend/tests/src/test/kotlin/io/tolgee/ee/service/translationMemory/TranslationMemoryTiebreakTest.kt"]}}
